course: dictionary
lesson: 13997
title: Lots and lots
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Lots» is a small word with a big job. Most often it means a large number or amount: «Mia has lots of friends at school.» You can count friends, so lots means many. You can also measure water, so «There was lots of water in the pool» means a large amount.
explain: Lots can also mean very much, especially in friendly, informal talk: «I feel lots better today.» Here lots works like an adverb, telling you how much better. Check by swapping in «much» or «a lot»: «I feel much better» still makes sense.
explain: Lots has other meanings too. Lot can be a piece of land or a thing sold at an auction, so lots is its plural. «Draw lots» means choose by chance, like picking slips of paper from a hat. In maths, «3 lots of 4» means 3 groups of 4, which is 12. The words around lots show you which meaning fits.
fact: Lots means a large number or amount, as in «lots of fun».
fact: As an adverb in informal speech, lots means very much: «lots better».
fact: «Lots of» is followed by a noun, such as «lots of books» or «lots of rain».
fact: «Draw lots» means choose by chance, often by picking slips of paper.
fact: «3 lots of 4» means 3 × 4 = 12, which is a good way to explain multiplying.
exercise: «We picked lots of apples from the orchard.» What does lots of mean here? | A single basket | Very sour | Only three apples | *A large number
exercise: «I feel lots better after my rest.» What does lots mean in this sentence? | *Very much | A large number of feelings | Not at all | Lots of times
exercise: «3 lots of 4 is 12.» What does 3 lots of 4 mean? | Three added to four | Four take away three | *Three groups of four | Four groups of twelve
test: «We will draw lots to decide who starts the game.» How are the children choosing who starts? | By voting for their favourite | By who is the tallest | By asking the teacher to pick | *By chance, like picking slips of paper
test: «There were lots of people at the fair, so the queue was long.» Which word means about the same as lots here? | Few | Empty | Quiet | *Many
exam: Which sentence uses lots as an adverb meaning very much? | *«Grandma says she feels lots better today.» | «Draw lots to choose the team captain.» | «There are lots of stars in the sky tonight.» | «We need lots of paint for the wall.»
